{"task_id": "Mbpp/414", "solution": "from typing import Iterable, Any\n\ndef overlapping(seq1: Iterable[Any], seq2: Iterable[Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if any value in `seq1` exists in `seq2` using Python's equality (`==`).\n    Returns `False` if either sequence is empty or no common elements are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not seq1 or not seq2:\n        return False\n\n    # Convert seq2 to a set for efficient O(1) average time lookups.\n    # This also handles cases where seq2 might be a one-shot iterable (e.g., generator).\n    set_seq2 = set(seq2)\n\n    for item1 in seq1:\n        if item1 in set_seq2:\n            return True\n            \n    return False"}
