{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "def check_smaller(tuple1, tuple2) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validate inputs and return True iff for every index i, tuple2[i] < tuple1[i].\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: if either input is not a tuple or if any pair of elements cannot be compared using '<'.\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if all tuple2[i] < tuple1[i], False otherwise (including unequal lengths).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"inputs must be tuples\")\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        return False\n    for a, b in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        try:\n            # Evaluate b < a (second compared to first)\n            if not (b < a):\n                return False\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # Map runtime comparability exceptions to TypeError per SRS BR7\n            raise TypeError(f\"elements not comparable using '<': {exc}\") from exc\n    return True"}
